# benchmark B5 : 400 particles, deposited and then left to settle
#
# B1-B4 all stop at 0.275 s of simulated time, which is before the packing
# settles.  Measured against them, the contact solver looks cheap; in a settled
# pile it is the whole cost.  A 2500-particle settled packing runs at about
# 34 ms/step against B2's 4 ms/step -- 8.5x -- so B1-B4 systematically
# under-report anything that speeds up contact detection.
#
# This case is the same phenomenon at a size that can still be iterated on:
# contact-dominated, but a run takes about half a minute rather than seven.
boxsize		1 1 1.2
boxcorner	0 0 0
density		1
Gravity		0   0   -10

outDt		0.05
timeStep	0.0001
maxTime		1.2

particleSize	0.06
particleSizeWidth 0.05
nParticle	400

stiffness	5e+02
damping		5e+0
friction	2.0e-1
cohesion	0.0

output		out
method		deposition
boundary	solid
eta		1.4
zeta		1.4
relaxation	0
